  "description": "Lepcha — spoken by the Lepcha people of Sikkim, Darjeeling district (West Bengal), and parts of Nepal and Bhutan; written in its own ancient Lepcha (Róng) script; among the older literary lineages of the eastern Himalayan frontier.  Three-way stop contrast at four places (voiceless / voiceless-aspirated / voiced) at bilabial, dental, palatal, velar.  Three nasals (m, n, ŋ).  Sibilant /s/, glottal /h/.  Standard liquid pair /l, r/.  Glides.  21 cells filled.",
